// Title: Gpresult Display Group Policy Information
// Sigma ID: e56d3073-83ff-4021-90fe-c658e0709e72
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-05-01 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1615
// Description: Detects cases in which a user uses the built-in Windows utility gpresult to display the
//   Resultant Set of Policy (RSoP) information
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1615/T1615.md
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/gpresult
//   - https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/emissary-trojan-changelog-did-operation-lotus-blossom-cause-it-to-evolve/
//   - https://www.welivesecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/ESET_Turla_ComRAT.pdf
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_gpresult_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\gpresult.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/z" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/v")
